# Simple OS – bootloader for the installed system (BIOS + UEFI), offline without a package pool on the medium.
# Only the parts that can be installed side by side; the meta packages grub-pc and grub-efi-amd64 exclude
# each other -> they are stored as .deb in /usr/share/simpleos/bootloader-debs (hook 08_bootloader_debs)
# and installed by /usr/sbin/bootloader-config depending on the firmware.
grub-common
# update-grub, grub-install
grub2-common
# BIOS (i386-pc) and UEFI (x86_64-efi)
grub-pc-bin
grub-efi-amd64-bin
# Secure Boot (on by default on current laptops): shim (signed by Microsoft) + GRUB signed by Debian;
# Calamares always installs them via /usr/local/sbin/simpleos-grub-install with --uefi-secure-boot. Without these
# packages the installed system got an unsigned GRUB and did not start with Secure Boot.
# mokutil: register keys for self-built modules (DKMS: nvidia-driver, broadcom-sta)
shim-signed
grub-efi-amd64-signed
mokutil
os-prober
efibootmgr
# Dependencies of the bundled .debs (grub-pc/grub-efi-amd64: ucf; cryptsetup-initramfs with LUKS)
ucf
cryptsetup
keyutils
initramfs-tools
